Owner patch — RiskManager.mqh:296 inverted OrderCalcMargin direction
=====================================================================
STATUS: OWNER-PENDING. NOT applied to the frozen mql5/ tree (anchor
227bf66); applying it is an owner-authority re-anchor step (new
source.commit + manifest + provenance, mission §26/§32). Prepared on Mac;
NOT compiled here.

Bug (confirmed by source review; PROGRESS.md 2026-09-16): a LONG stop sits
BELOW entry (price > slPrice), a SHORT stop ABOVE (price < slPrice), so the
direction inferred for the OrderCalcMargin side-selection was INVERTED.

Impact (bounded): nil on symmetric-margin FX; on instruments with
asymmetric long/short margin the wrong side is queried, so required margin
— and thus margin-scaled volume — can be computed against the wrong side.
Never bypasses the SL; never affects symmetric symbols.

Apply from the repo root (on the checkout being re-anchored):
    git apply owner_patches/RiskManager_296_direction.patch

Regression: tests/test_riskmanager_direction_patch.py pins the correct
direction logic and verifies this patch flips `<` to `>` at line 296.
--- 8< --- unified diff below --- 8< ---
diff --git a/mql5/Include/Mql5Bot/RiskManager.mqh b/mql5/Include/Mql5Bot/RiskManager.mqh
index 1b5dfed..4b430eb 100644
--- a/mql5/Include/Mql5Bot/RiskManager.mqh
+++ b/mql5/Include/Mql5Bot/RiskManager.mqh
@@ -293,7 +293,11 @@ public:
         }
 
       //---- margin check (query, never assume — SPEC §3.3) ---------------
-      long dir = (price < slPrice) ? POSITION_TYPE_LONG : POSITION_TYPE_SHORT;
+      // LONG stops sit BELOW entry (price > slPrice); SHORT stops sit
+      // ABOVE (price < slPrice). Infer the side from that geometry so
+      // OrderCalcMargin queries the correct side on asymmetric-margin
+      // instruments (fix 2026-09; was inverted `price < slPrice`).
+      long dir = (price > slPrice) ? POSITION_TYPE_LONG : POSITION_TYPE_SHORT;
       double margin = 0.0;
       if(!OrderCalcMargin((dir == POSITION_TYPE_LONG) ? ORDER_TYPE_BUY
                                                       : ORDER_TYPE_SELL,
